research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-r3-subsequences-fs.log-6371-items/rem-completeness-routes.md:88:and, through the peak lemma, Bolzano-Weierstrass
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-r3-subsequences-fs.log-6372-items/rem-completeness-routes.md:89:([[thm-bolzano-weierstrass]]), which gives the Cauchy criterion
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-r3-subsequences-fs.log-6373-items/lem-subsequence-inherits-limit.md:85:- The divergence test is the standard way to show a concrete sequence diverges, and it is how [[fs-bounded-implies-convergent]] is refuted. The opposite direction, extracting a convergent subsequence from a bounded sequence, is Bolzano-Weierstrass; it is **not proved anywhere in this library as things stand**, being the subject of the next page of this track, planned and not yet written.
